compat-include/ -- glibc >= 2.41 vs CUDA 13.0 header clash
==========================================================

glibc 2.41 added the C23 reciprocal-square-root functions to <bits/mathcalls.h>:

    __MATHCALL_VEC (rsqrt,, (_Mdouble_ __x));     /* line 206 in glibc 2.43 */

which expands to `rsqrt`/`rsqrtf`/`rsqrtl` declared `noexcept (true)`. CUDA 13.0's
crt/math_functions.h (lines 629 / 653) declares the same three names as
`__device_builtin__` WITHOUT an exception specification. nvcc's front end rejects the
pair outright:

    error: exception specification is incompatible with that of previous function "rsqrt"

so gpu_loop.cu does not compile at all on such a box. CUDA fixed this on its side after
13.0, but 13.0 is a CEILING here, not a floor -- these binaries link cudart statically and
a 13.1+ build demands a driver newer than the validators' 580.x, so it would not start at
all (install-env.sh header).

The fix therefore goes on the glibc side. bits/mathcalls.h here is a byte-identical copy of
/usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu/bits/mathcalls.h with that ONE declaration commented out;
build.sh puts this directory on -I ahead of the system paths, and only when a probe compile
actually fails.

Why not -D: the guard is `#if __GLIBC_USE (IEC_60559_FUNCS_EXT_C23)`, and
bits/libc-header-start.h #undefs that macro and re-derives it from __USE_GNU -- which g++
always defines. A -D on the command line does not survive.

Why not a -include shim that renames the symbols: nvcc's own pre-includes (cuda_runtime.h)
are processed before any -include file, so <math.h> is already through by then. Measured.

Host code in gpu_loop.cu does not call rsqrt/rsqrtf/rsqrtl, so dropping the host
declaration costs nothing; device code gets them from CUDA as before.

Regenerate after a glibc upgrade:

    sed '206s|^__MATHCALL_VEC (rsqrt,, (_Mdouble_ __x));$|/* suppressed */|' \
        /usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu/bits/mathcalls.h > compat-include/bits/mathcalls.h

and check the line number still matches -- diff against the system header must show
exactly one changed line.
